================================================================================
Third-party code
================================================================================

The @revkit/components package vendors copy-in source from permissive-licensed
upstreams (see docs/adr/0022-vendored-code-licenses.md). Each vendored drop
lives in its own subdirectory beside the vendor README, with the upstream
LICENSE file and an UPSTREAM provenance file that records repo, commit, path
and the declared SPDX license.

The `revkit check` vendored-code guard enforces every STRUCTURAL rule (UPSTREAM
key shape, `https://` repo with a host, full-40-char commit SHA, permitted
SPDX id, layout, symlink refusal, NOTICE format), and requires that each
entry below points at a real subdirectory whose UPSTREAM `license:` equals
the entry's SPDX id.

The LICENSE bytes themselves are gated by CODEOWNERS
(`.github/CODEOWNERS`, `packages/components/vendor/` + `NOTICE` require the
maintainer's review) rather than by a hand-rolled canonical-text matcher —
an SPDX-template matcher that admits real upstream LICENSE variance
(curly quotes, per-line comment prefixes, condensed paragraphs) while
refusing adversarial appends belongs behind a well-tested library.

Entries take the form (one per line, at the start of the line):

    - packages/components/vendor/<pkg> — <upstream URL> (SPDX: <id>)

No third-party code is vendored yet.
